<article class="ed-guide bg-canvas py-12 md:py-16" aria-label="Test a new printer and scanner"><div class="ed-layout">
{{ contents([{"id": "start", "title": "Find your starting point"}, {"id": "print-one-page", "title": "Print one page"}, {"id": "scan-one-item", "title": "Scan one item"}, {"id": "record-what-you-found", "title": "Record what you found"}, {"id": "separate-next-steps", "title": "Choose the next step"}, {"id": "related", "title": "What to read next"}]) }}
<div class="ed-reading guide-reading text-lg">
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Testing should answer a small practical question: can the chosen device send an ordinary print job, and can the multifunction printer create and save a basic scan? Use harmless material, check the result, and record the limits of the test. A successful test does not prove that every paper size, application, network condition or hardware feature will work.</p>
<section class="ed-start" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-heading"><p class="ed-label">Start here</p><h2 id="start-heading">Use a small, repeatable check</h2><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Test printing first, then scanning if the equipment supports it. Keep the result and notes separate from any broader fault investigation.</p><div class="ed-choices">
{{ choice("Print one page", "Choose ordinary paper, a clear document and the intended printer. Check legibility, orientation, size and margins.", "#print-one-page", "startup", "/img/guides/printer-field-guide-v1.webp", "A household printer with a sheet of paper.", "Read this part") }}
{{ choice("Scan one item", "Use official supported software, save one harmless scan to the intended folder, and open the saved file.", "#scan-one-item", "applications", "/img/guides/printer-field-guide-v1.webp", "A laptop and connection cable.", "Read this part") }}
{{ choice("Record the boundary", "Note what worked, what was not tested and any visible issue without treating the check as a full diagnostic.", "#record-what-you-found", "online", "/img/guides/printer-field-guide-v1.webp", "A magnifying glass over a printed test page.", "Read this part") }}
</div></section>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="print-one-page"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span>Print one page</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Choose a harmless document and the paper type already loaded. In the print dialogue, select the intended printer, paper size, orientation and one copy. Avoid changing several settings at once.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">After printing, check that the text is legible, the page is the expected size and orientation, and the margins are sensible. Look for obvious smears, missing areas or unexpected blank pages. If the result is not right, record the selected settings and the visible result before trying another change.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="scan-one-item"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Scan one item</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If the printer includes a scanner, place one harmless item according to the manufacturer’s instructions. Use the official supported scanning software, select the available source and output options, and save the result to the intended folder.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Open the saved file and check that it can be viewed, that the whole item is present and that it is readable at a practical size. Windows users can refer to <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/hardware/printer/install-and-use-a-scanner-in-windows">Microsoft’s scanner instructions</a> for the supported scanning workflow.</p>{% call note("care", "Take care", "keep private material out of a first test") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Use a harmless page rather than identity documents, financial records or private correspondence. A basic test should not create unnecessary copies of sensitive information.</p>{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="record-what-you-found"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>Record what you found</h2>
<div class="mb-8 overflow-x-auto" role="region" aria-label="New Printer Setup reference" tabindex="0"><table role="table" class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm md:text-base"><thead><tr><th scope="col" class="border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-bold text-ink">Item</th><th scope="col" class="border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-bold text-ink">Check</th><th scope="col" class="border border-line bg-surface p-4 font-bold text-ink">Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label="Item" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Print</td><td data-label="Check" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">One page is legible and correctly sized</td><td data-label="Meaning" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">The selected device completed this ordinary print check</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Item" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Scan</td><td data-label="Check" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">A saved file opens and shows the full item</td><td data-label="Meaning" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">The basic scan-and-save path worked for this test</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Item" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Untested</td><td data-label="Check" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">Other apps, sizes, features or devices</td><td data-label="Meaning" class="border border-line p-4 align-top text-muted">No conclusion has been made about those conditions</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Write down the printer model, device used, connection type, date and result. Record anything not tested. Do not describe a single successful page or scan as a full warranty assessment or proof that the hardware has no faults.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="separate-next-steps"><span aria-hidden="true">04</span>Choose the next step</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If the basic check fails, preserve the visible error and the settings used. Re-read the exact model instructions before making repeated changes. A problem with an application, network, paper path or queue may need a different investigation from a problem with the printer itself.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Keep this test separate from broader printer fault diagnosis. Do not disassemble the equipment or force trays, covers or cartridges. If a result is unsafe, unusual or unclear, stop using the printer until the relevant instructions or appropriate support have been checked.</p>
